    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, carrying a commanding score of 81.88. He faces the vulnerable Ryan Johnson (xERA 5.15), and the confluence of a favorable platoon advantage and a premium batting order position makes him our primary offensive engine. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.86) remain elite start requirements; while **Jackson Merrill** faces the risk of an elite catcher\u2019s arm hindering his stolen base potential, his underlying power-speed profile against the subpar stuff of JR Ritchie is too valuable to suppress. **Andy Pages** (72.83) also benefits significantly from the matchup against Kendry Rojas, as the SP skill gap pushes his efficiency well into our \"Strong\" tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s bench was **Josh Jung**, who landed at 53.10. While he offers a higher floor than **Dominic Smith** (44.10), the optimizer prioritized **Dominic Smith**\u2019s roster flexibility and the total daily cap management strategy over a marginal gain in raw projected output. We continue to monitor the status of **Nasim Nunez**; despite his elite speed, the matchup against the difficult Luzardo pushed his score down to 41.20, keeping him on the pine to protect our overall game caps. **Jacob Wilson** remains an intriguing \"Strong\" start at 67.10, buoyed by favorable wind conditions that add a crucial 5% boost to his projection, helping him outperform our depth options like **Miguel Vargas** and **Curtis Mead**.\n\nBe advised that today\u2019s lineup remains speculative until official cards are posted. **Drake Baldwin** and **Nolan Schanuel** are currently projected on the fringe of our starting requirements; should their confirmed batting orders slide down the lineup, their efficiency scores\u2014already hovering near the 56.0 mark\u2014will be re-evaluated to ensure we aren't burning valuable starts on declining opportunities. We are leaning heavily into the platoon edges afforded to **Jacob Wilson** and **Andy Pages** today to capitalize on weak SP metrics, keeping our eyes peeled for any late-breaking weather patterns that might shift these projections.",
